        "content": "## 1. Insiemi, parametri e variabili decisionali\n\n### Insiemi\n\n- Nodi:\n  \\[\n  N=\\{S,A,B,C,T\\}.\n  \\]\n\n- Archi attivabili:\n  \\[\n  E=\\{(S,A),(S,B),(A,B),(A,C),(B,C),(B,T),(C,T)\\}.\n  \\]\n\n### Parametri\n\nPer ogni arco \\((i,j)\\in E\\):\n\n- \\(F_{ij}\\): costo fisso di attivazione;\n- \\(c_{ij}\\): costo unitario di trasporto;\n- \\(U_{ij}\\): capacità.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccc}\n(i,j) & F_{ij} & c_{ij} & U_{ij}\\\\ \\hline\n(S,A)&40&2&30\\\\\n(S,B)&35&3&35\\\\\n(A,B)&15&1&15\\\\\n(A,C)&30&2&25\\\\\n(B,C)&18&2&20\\\\\n(B,T)&45&4&25\\\\\n(C,T)&38&2&35\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBilancio netto dei nodi:\n\n\\[\nb_S=40,\\qquad b_T=-40,\\qquad b_A=b_B=b_C=0.\n\\]\n\n### Variabili decisionali\n\nPer ogni \\((i,j)\\in E\\):\n\n- \\(x_{ij}\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge 0}\\): flusso intero inviato sull’arco \\((i,j)\\);\n- \\(y_{ij}\\in\\{0,1\\}\\): vale 1 se l’arco \\((i,j)\\) è attivato.\n\nNel codice, le variabili sono denominate `x_i_j` e `y_i_j`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Formulazione matematica completa\n\n### Funzione obiettivo\n\n\\[\n\\min \\sum_{(i,j)\\in E}\\left(F_{ij}y_{ij}+c_{ij}x_{ij}\\right).\n\\]\n\nEsplicitamente:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\min\\quad\n&40y_{SA}+35y_{SB}+15y_{AB}+30y_{AC}+18y_{BC}+45y_{BT}+38y_{CT}\\\\\n&+2x_{SA}+3x_{SB}+x_{AB}+2x_{AC}+2x_{BC}+4x_{BT}+2x_{CT}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n### Conservazione del flusso\n\nIn forma generale:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{j:(i,j)\\in E}x_{ij}\n-\n\\sum_{j:(j,i)\\in E}x_{ji}\n=b_i\n\\qquad \\forall i\\in N.\n\\]\n\nEquivalentemente:\n\n\\[\nx_{SA}+x_{SB}=40,\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_{AB}+x_{AC}-x_{SA}=0,\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_{BC}+x_{BT}-x_{SB}-x_{AB}=0,\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_{CT}-x_{AC}-x_{BC}=0,\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_{BT}+x_{CT}=40.\n\\]\n\n### Capacità e attivazione\n\n\\[\nx_{ij}\\le U_{ij}y_{ij}\n\\qquad \\forall (i,j)\\in E.\n\\]\n\n### Domini\n\n\\[\nx_{ij}\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge 0}\n\\qquad \\forall(i,j)\\in E,\n\\]\n\n\\[\ny_{ij}\\in\\{0,1\\}\n\\qquad \\forall(i,j)\\in E.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n## 3. Codice Python con Gurobi\n\n```python\nimport gurobipy as gp\nfrom gurobipy import GRB\nimport json\n\nnodes = [\"S\", \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"T\"]\n\narcs = [\n    (\"S\", \"A\"),\n    (\"S\", \"B\"),\n    (\"A\", \"B\"),\n    (\"A\", \"C\"),\n    (\"B\", \"C\"),\n    (\"B\", \"T\"),\n    (\"C\", \"T\"),\n]\n\nfixed_cost = {\n    (\"S\", \"A\"): 40,\n    (\"S\", \"B\"): 35,\n    (\"A\", \"B\"): 15,\n    (\"A\", \"C\"): 30,\n    (\"B\", \"C\"): 18,\n    (\"B\", \"T\"): 45,\n    (\"C\", \"T\"): 38,\n}\n\nunit_cost = {\n    (\"S\", \"A\"): 2,\n    (\"S\", \"B\"): 3,\n    (\"A\", \"B\"): 1,\n    (\"A\", \"C\"): 2,\n    (\"B\", \"C\"): 2,\n    (\"B\", \"T\"): 4,\n    (\"C\", \"T\"): 2,\n}\n\ncapacity = {\n    (\"S\", \"A\"): 30,\n    (\"S\", \"B\"): 35,\n    (\"A\", \"B\"): 15,\n    (\"A\", \"C\"): 25,\n    (\"B\", \"C\"): 20,\n    (\"B\", \"T\"): 25,\n    (\"C\", \"T\"): 35,\n}\n\nbalance = {\n    \"S\": 40,\n    \"A\": 0,\n    \"B\": 0,\n    \"C\": 0,\n    \"T\": -40,\n}\n\nenv = gp.Env(empty=True)\nenv.setParam(\"OutputFlag\", 0)\nenv.start()\n\nmodel = gp.Model(\"M10_rete_distributiva\", env=env)\n\nx = {\n    (i, j): model.addVar(\n        lb=0,\n        ub=capacity[i, j],\n        vtype=GRB.INTEGER,\n        name=f\"x_{i}_{j}\"\n    )\n    for i, j in arcs\n}\n\ny = {\n    (i, j): model.addVar(\n        vtype=GRB.BINARY,\n        name=f\"y_{i}_{j}\"\n    )\n    for i, j in arcs\n}\n\nmodel.setObjective(\n    gp.quicksum(\n        fixed_cost[i, j] * y[i, j] + unit_cost[i, j] * x[i, j]\n        for i, j in arcs\n    ),\n    GRB.MINIMIZE\n)\n\nfor node in nodes:\n    outgoing = gp.quicksum(x[i, j] for i, j in arcs if i == node)\n    incoming = gp.quicksum(x[i, j] for i, j in arcs if j == node)\n    model.addConstr(\n        outgoing - incoming == balance[node],\n        name=f\"balance_{node}\"\n    )\n\nfor i, j in arcs:\n    model.addConstr(\n        x[i, j] <= capacity[i, j] * y[i, j],\n        name=f\"activation_{i}_{j}\"\n    )\n\nmodel.optimize()\n\nstatus_names = {\n    1: \"LOADED\",\n    2: \"OPTIMAL\",\n    3: \"INFEASIBLE\",\n    4: \"INF_OR_UNBD\",\n    5: \"UNBOUNDED\",\n    6: \"CUTOFF\",\n    7: \"ITERATION_LIMIT\",\n    8: \"NODE_LIMIT\",\n    9: \"TIME_LIMIT\",\n    10: \"SOLUTION_LIMIT\",\n    11: \"INTERRUPTED\",\n    12: \"NUMERIC\",\n    13: \"SUBOPTIMAL\",\n    14: \"INPROGRESS\",\n    15: \"USER_OBJ_LIMIT\",\n    16: \"WORK_LIMIT\",\n    17: \"MEM_LIMIT\",\n}\n\nstatus = status_names.get(model.Status, f\"STATUS_{model.Status}\")\n\nif model.Status == GRB.OPTIMAL:\n    def numeric_value(value):\n        rounded = round(value)\n        if abs(value - rounded) <= 1e-6:\n            return float(rounded)\n        return float(value)\n\n    variable_values = {}\n    for i, j in arcs:\n        variable_values[f\"x_{i}_{j}\"] = numeric_value(x[i, j].X)\n    for i, j in arcs:\n        variable_values[f\"y_{i}_{j}\"] = numeric_value(y[i, j].X)\n\n    result = {\n        \"status\": status,\n        \"objective\": numeric_value(model.ObjVal),\n        \"variables\": variable_values,\n    }\nelse:\n    result = {\n        \"status\": status,\n        \"objective\": None,\n        \"variables\": {},\n    }\n\nprint(\"SOLUTION_JSON=\" + json.dumps(result, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n```\n\n## 4. Sintesi della soluzione\n\nLo stato è **OPTIMAL** e il costo minimo è:\n\n\\[\nz^*=443.\n\\]\n\nFlussi non nulli:\n\n\\[\nx_{SA}=25,\\quad x_{SB}=15,\\quad x_{AC}=25,\\quad\nx_{BT}=15,\\quad x_{CT}=25.\n\\]\n\nArchi attivati:\n\n\\[\ny_{SA}=y_{SB}=y_{AC}=y_{BT}=y_{CT}=1.\n\\]\n\nGli archi \\(A\\to B\\) e \\(B\\to C\\) non sono attivati. Il costo è composto da 188 unità di costi fissi e 255 unità di costi di trasporto.",
